# Molex_430450418 — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC pinned
# in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# MOTOR PHASE HEADER: Molex Micro-Fit 3.0, 2x2 (dual row), 3.00 mm pitch,
# surface mount, VERTICAL. 8.5 A per contact, 600 V, -40 °C to +105 °C.
#
# WHY THIS PART AND NOT THE 2 mm PA FAMILY (Ben, 2026-09-04): the brief requires
# >=6 A phase pins and notes that a NEMA23 at ~4 A RMS exceeds a 3 A connector;
# every JST PA part is 3 A. The PA family is also rated only to +85 °C, and the
# sealed Middleweight case is designed to a 100 °C worst-case ambient, so the PA
# parts sit outside their rating there. This is the only vertical SMT candidate
# found that clears both. Cost: it stands ~9.9 mm proud of the board (the PA is
# ~6 mm), so it sets lid clearance - accepted by Ben, same day.
#
# Pins: 1 and 2 are one row, 3 and 4 the other; 5 and 6 are the board tabs
# (mechanical, tie to gnd). Phase A takes one row, phase B the other, so each
# phase's pair stays together in the connector and in the loom.
# Pinned 2026-09-04: LCSC C293535, Extended, 11394 in stock, $0.98.

p1 = io("p1", Net, optional = True)
p2 = io("p2", Net, optional = True)
p3 = io("p3", Net, optional = True)
p4 = io("p4", Net, optional = True)
tab1 = io("tab1", Net, optional = True)
tab2 = io("tab2", Net, optional = True)

Component(
    name = "Molex_430450418",
    footprint = File("Molex_430450418/CONN-SMD_430450418.kicad_mod"),
    symbol = Symbol("Molex_430450418/430450418.kicad_sym"),
    prefix = "J",
    part = Part(mpn = "43045-0418", manufacturer = "Molex"),
    properties = {"LCSC": "C293535", "MPN": "430450418"},
    pins = {
        "1": p1,
        "2": p2,
        "3": p3,
        "4": p4,
        "5": tab1,
        "6": tab2,
    },
)
